      choices: ['Re-hear all the witnesses and decide the facts again', 'Review errors of law or procedure, and safety of the conviction — not simply re-weigh the evidence', 'Re-prosecute from scratch', 'Consult the jury foreperson'],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'Appeals are about law, process and safety, not a second bite at the facts — the trial court saw the witnesses, the appellate court only the transcript.',
