      choices: ['The judge', 'The jury of twelve, on the judge\'s directions of law', 'The prosecutor', 'The magistrates sitting behind'],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'Facts go to the jury, law to the judge — the classical division. In civil trials the judge usually does both jobs alone.',
